{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779209244,"nonce":"cIZ+CP62G10j6I0t8a2i158FJxA=","message":"## Current core Feedbax open-issue map for the Studio/Mandible overhaul\n\nThis is the core-library counterpart to the Studio map on `93f79f2`. It cross-references the open issues that currently matter to making Studio and Mandible operate over durable Feedbax contracts instead of UI-local metadata.\n\nProvider, manifests, lineage, and Mandible boundary:\n- `c6c6da0` — Feedbax manifests and provider contract remains the central spec for provider schemas, registries, validation, artifact refs, and standalone/Mandible-compatible operation.\n- `f68cf66` — expose Feedbax as a Mandible plugin/provider.\n- `e33f487` — run manifests as canonical lineage with database indexing.\n- `5f22fa7` and `bdee8d1` — project routing/registration and research-app integration patterns.\n- `fa3978f` remains the closed roadmap ledger for the cross-repo MVP phases and should still be read first for Mandible/Feedbax ownership boundaries.\n\nExecution, lowering, and backend correctness:\n- `e57ae1f` — real Studio training backend over actual JAX training/eval/analysis.\n- `3fae4f8` — analytical lowering interface.\n- `d64a9aa` — environment/task protocol unification, including evaluation variants and input/port overrides.\n- `c39271a`, `e919d5d`, `323de09`, `d999dea`, and `f451fc4` — model input/intervenor/task/model interface questions that affect lowering and introspection.\n- `e08aeb5`, `ae2d692`, `96a0725`, `29c89d8`, and `9b97528` — backend/runtime correctness issues around model copies, checkpoints, JAX static metadata, and `SimpleFeedbackState` documentation/redesign.\n- `cc62b31` — TPU multiprocessing lockfile race.\n\nTask, state, selector, and metric contracts:\n- `85cec2c` — runtime/schema-backed state browser should eventually expose arbitrary PyTree paths, shapes, dtypes, axis labels, units/frames, and selector validation.\n- `e5a1e6c` — task-aware metric columns need durable metric/task/objective/analysis specs or provider outputs.\n- `b3ad156`, `7c0c4b2`, `0e1cd8c`, and `0258fac` — flexible state targeting, selector APIs, probe/metric nodes, and typed ports.\n- `c540499` and `3fc3e8e` — lazy task generation and adaptive-length trials.\n\nAnalysis and scientific-product backend:\n- `e8452a4` — move analysis layer into Feedbax with controller protocol, graph-step adapter, LTV/LTI linearisation, and induced-gain tools.\n- `d67e303`, `8d4097e`, and `40f8322` — cross-timestep loss support, unified difference-loss family, and multi-run loss plotting.\n- `b2db05b`, `c722539`, and `4cb86c8` — statistics tab backend/frontend/product slices.\n\nComponent/model architecture and palettes:\n- `6116155`, `2f8dd61`, `a6efafc`, `ba00cef`, `f90e6e2`, `6fe14ab`, and `fe093fc` — typed subgraphs, parametric composites, acausal systems, alternate training methods, morphology, and MJX plant integration.\n- `4178e12`, `afff745`, `c77b227`, `44183de`, and `d0cc2b7` — graph-as-model, subgraph navigation/races, Network wiring/round-trip cleanup, LSTM execution, and registry/builder mismatch issues.\n\nRecent fixture correction: the RLRMP seeded graph now uses generalized `DelayedReaches` with `train_endpoint_mode='center_out'` rather than `SimpleReaches`. That is a small core contract improvement because the task object can now express the delayed center-out training endpoint mode used by RLRMP, while the richer eval override model remains tracked by `0c46f69`/`d64a9aa`/`e57ae1f`.","files":null}]}